Z||000000||87 Pegasus||10-09-2001||12:13 AM||||At 2:30 pm in the Northwestern Subburbs of Chicago 2 F-16's where dispatched to escort an American Airliner to O'Hare International Airport.  The 2 F-16's flying at the speed of sound (600 + mph) caused a Sonic Boom heard nearly 20-30 miles away.  when it happened it sounded like a missile or bomb had gone off..shaking building and shattering windows...  The scare was just a mentaling handicaped man roughly 30 years old saying that the plane was going to fly into the Sears Tower and it was up to him to stop this from happening so he jumped out of his seat and rushed to the Cockpit down and broke through it. passengers rushed to aid the pilots and bring down the man.  All it well now in Chicago but it was a scare.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1367_3.gif"> <BR>God Bless America....<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!||||reg||9
