Z||000006||SteveJ||10-09-2001||09:47 AM||||Very few people born in the 60's or later have heard a sonic boom. They were occasional when jets were new but were annoying and so banned.<P>That anti-noise policy is what killed the Concord.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cheever3000||10-09-2001||10:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I didn't hear any sonic booms.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>You have to be along the flight path at the time they are going that speed.  Could be they slowed by the time they reached your location, or you weren't close enough to the path they took.  When the Space Shuttle crosses Houston to land in Florida, it makes a sonic boom, but I've been here 2 years and still haven't heard it, even the time I saw it blazing across the night sky.  I remember growing up not far from Tinker AFB and hearing sonic booms every day.  Shakes the house but you get used to it.  I can understand why it would rattle someone who's "uneducated" to it.<P>||||reg||1
